  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Securing Human Investments to Foster Transformation II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objective of the second DPO in the series is to continue to (i) strengthen CRVS, health and education systems essential for HC accumulation; (ii) recognize the contribution of women to economic productivity; and (iii) improve national safety nets to respond to shocks in a more efficient manner.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objectives of the Second Securing Human Investments to Foster Transformation Development Policy Financing in Pakistan are to continue to: (i) strengthen civil registration and vital statistics (CRVS), health and education systems essential for human capital accumulation; (ii) recognize the contribution of women to economic productivity; and (iii) improve national safety nets to respond to shocks in a more efficient manner. The policy program is organized under three pillars. Pillar A supports policy actions to improve access to and efficiency of CRVS systems, improve quality of and access to health services, support data driven decision-making to improve the quality of education and reduce the proportion of children who are out of school. Pillar A also supports improved efficiency of budget use and predictability of financing for basic and essential health services. Pillar B supports policy reforms to recognize the contribution of female informal workers to economic productivity and increase the potential for labor force participation of women by improving their work environments and working conditions. Pillar C supports policy actions to expand the ownership and improve governance of National Socio-Economic Registry to help it transform into a fully integrated national social registry. This is expected to lead to a more effective coordination and decision-making tool for targeting social programs, including social safety nets and other social protection initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
